<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maurice Bishop International Airport</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1984">1984</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Point Salines International Airport</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop">Maurice Bishop</a> International Airport, formerly Point Salines International Airport, is the main airport of Grenada, at the south-western tip of the island. Its construction under Maurice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a>'s government with Cuban workers was seen by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> as a possible military threat and was cited to justify the invasion of 1983. It opened in 1984 and was renamed after Bishop in 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop-international-airport.jpg" alt="Maurice Bishop International Airport" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Estormiz · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maurice_Bishop_International_Airport_Grenada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
